From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa: cc_test clear teardown quiesce delay (T-M6-8 R4c)

The R4b silicon test wedged the board when 'clear <port>' was immediately
followed by a VyOS vif-config commit. The clear path already detaches the CC
graft and clears FMBM_RCCB before freeing MURAM (correct order, F-134), but
freed the CC/HMTD MURAM with no drain window. F-135/F-136 established that
freeing live-walked FMan MURAM before in-flight tasks quiesce can bus-lock the
controller. Insert the proven ~5 ms DPAA1 drain between clearing RCCB and
fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy(). Also documents the operational rule (do not churn
VyOS config on the port during teardown). Debug harness only; no production
path change.

Signed-off-by: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c
index 1bcc1f0..da12bc1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/seq_file.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
@@ -544,6 +545,10 @@ static ssize_t cc_test_write(struct file *file, const char __user *buf,
 		rxport = fman_port_lookup_rx(fman_pcd_get_fman(pcd), port_id);
 		if (rxport)
 			(void)fman_port_set_cc_base(rxport, 0);
+		/* R4c teardown hardening: detach + clear RCCB first, then let
+		 * in-flight FMan tasks drain before freeing live-walked MURAM.
+		 * F-135/F-136 proved that freeing before drain can bus-lock FMan. */
+		usleep_range(5000, 6000);
 		fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy(pcd, port_id);
 		if (port_id < ARRAY_SIZE(cc_test_vlan_hm) &&
 		    cc_test_vlan_hm[port_id]) {
